BT 0.100 0.110 0.130 rg /F1 9.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 42.00 744.29 Tm (The projection starts from the last recorded balance and walks forward one day at a time. For each day: opening balance,) Tj ET
BT 0.100 0.110 0.130 rg /F1 9.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 42.00 731.59 Tm (plus income landing that day, minus obligations landing that day, equals closing balance, which becomes the next day's) Tj ET
BT 0.100 0.110 0.130 rg /F1 9.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 42.00 718.89 Tm (opening. Income is ordered before outflows within a day, because assuming the reverse would flag a phantom shortfall) Tj ET
BT 0.100 0.110 0.130 rg /F1 9.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 42.00 706.19 Tm (on every payday. No allowance for everyday spending is charged. All money is handled as exact decimal, rounded half) Tj ET
BT 0.100 0.110 0.130 rg /F1 9.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 42.00 693.49 Tm (up; floating point is never used, because a projection is a long chain of additions.) Tj ET
BT 0.100 0.110 0.130 rg /F1 9.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 42.00 673.79 Tm (Occurrence dates come from one calendar module used by every other part of the system, so the report and the app) Tj ET
BT 0.100 0.110 0.130 rg /F1 9.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 42.00 661.09 Tm (cannot drift apart. Monthly bills clamp to the last day of a short month. Weekly and biweekly items step 7 or 14 days from) Tj ET
BT 0.100 0.110 0.130 rg /F1 9.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 42.00 648.39 Tm (an anchor date, which is what makes a biweekly mortgage produce 26 payments a year rather than 24. Nothing is shifted) Tj ET
BT 0.100 0.110 0.130 rg /F1 9.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 42.00 635.69 Tm (off a weekend: a due date landing on a Saturday is counted on the Saturday, because shifting it to Monday would make) Tj ET
BT 0.100 0.110 0.130 rg /F1 9.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 42.00 622.99 Tm (the projection optimistic on precisely the days that matter.) Tj ET
BT 0.100 0.110 0.130 rg /F1 9.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 42.00 603.29 Tm (Optimisation works on episodes. The first stretch of days closing below the floor is identified, and its deficit is the amount) Tj ET
BT 0.100 0.110 0.130 rg /F1 9.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 42.00 590.59 Tm (that must be kept out of it. Candidates are obligations landing on or before the end of that stretch whose recorded window) Tj ET
BT 0.100 0.110 0.130 rg /F1 9.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 42.00 577.89 Tm (permits landing after it. They are taken least-critical first and largest first, so the fewest moves close the gap, and any) Tj ET
BT 0.100 0.110 0.130 rg /F1 9.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 42.00 565.19 Tm (move the episode turns out not to need is then dropped. The curve is re-run and the next episode examined, until none) Tj ET
BT 0.100 0.110 0.130 rg /F1 9.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 42.00 552.49 Tm (remain or nothing legitimate is left to move.) Tj ET
BT 0.100 0.110 0.130 rg /F1 9.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 42.00 532.79 Tm (Moving a payment later is safe for the balance curve in a precise sense: shifting an obligation from day d to day t raises) Tj ET
BT 0.100 0.110 0.130 rg /F1 9.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 42.00 520.09 Tm (every day from d to t-1 by its amount and changes no day from t onward, because the money has left by then either way.) Tj ET
BT 0.100 0.110 0.130 rg /F1 9.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 42.00 507.39 Tm (So a later date never worsens any day. The entire cost of moving is the risk of paying late, which is why a recorded) Tj ET
BT 0.100 0.110 0.130 rg /F1 9.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 42.00 494.69 Tm (deadline is required before this report will propose it.) Tj ET
BT 0.100 0.110 0.130 rg /F1 9.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 42.00 474.99 Tm (Total outflow is identical before and after optimisation, and that is asserted in the test suite rather than assumed. A) Tj ET
BT 0.100 0.110 0.130 rg /F1 9.50 Tf 1 0 0 1 42.00 462.29 Tm (schedule that reduces what is owed is not a schedule.) Tj ET
